Soldier ants. We all know them and hate them. They are the bane of NAO
players everywhere.

So what if you could play as one? No, not one ant, but one *swarm*.

Yes, I know it's crazy. I'm not even sure how you'd control such a
beast. And how would you "armor" a soldier ant? Maybe it's a swarm of
migo drones or some other lovecraftian monster. I guess swarm control
would go something like this:
1. You can name soldiers. This name is their group name, not an
individual name.
2. You can give orders to a group with the same name. These could be
simple "move_to" orders, explore orders, attack with prejudice, etc.
3. You can take control of any single guy to execute precision orders.
4. You can "tag" certain monsters or items as targets.
There would be a shared inventory across all ants for simplicity's
sake.

I'm not sure how controlling such a beast(s) would fit within the
general play scheme of Nethack. Here's my ideas on how to accomodate
some of the central play features:
1. Resistances
Females can occasionally be ordered to lay eggs. These have the same
resistances as their parent.
These resistances will *not* include MR/ reflection. Wand/touch of
death will deal massive damage.
As a compromise, perhaps high-level ants can cast a short-lived
reflection spell, or the quest artifact provides reflection for part
of the swarm when invoked.
2. armor
Your troops will put on uncursed armor as if they were pets. They
can't wear body armor.
3. death
Um, when does a "swarm" die? When all the females die.
4. EXP
Each individual troop has an EXP depending on how developed it is.
There's also a "hive mind" exp that slowly gains XP based on the
vicissitudes of its soldiers for to-hit and spellcasting purposes. A
potion of gain level is offered to the hive mind, so the hive gains XP
rather than any troop.

This idea is quite plainly a can-of-worms at best, an entirely
different game at worst. But for some reason I think it might make for
a fun game - it's certainly "different"!


